  "summary_en": "The UK's ten-year National AI Strategy, built on three pillars: investing in the AI ecosystem, spreading AI benefits across sectors and regions, and governing AI in a pro-innovation way. It favours a sector-led regulatory approach, with a 2022 White Paper to follow. Robotics and autonomous vehicles get only passing mention.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Three pillars: invest in the AI ecosystem, diffuse AI across sectors and regions, govern AI effectively.",
   "Commits to a White Paper in early 2022 on UK AI governance, testing sector-led regulation against alternatives.",
   "Pilots an AI Standards Hub and backs UK leadership in ISO/IEC and other AI standards.",
   "Publishes a CDEI AI assurance roadmap and develops a cross-government algorithmic transparency standard.",
   "Launches a UKRI National AI Research and Innovation Programme and new visa routes for AI talent."
